# November 22, 2026: South Dakota, a second statewide scatter (the emptiest state on the map that day, 35 places).
# Away from the ground the two earlier batches covered: Lemmon on the North Dakota line, Mobridge and Selby on the upper
# Missouri, Fort Pierre, Wessington Springs, Milbank and Stockholm by the Minnesota line, Brookings, Vermillion, and in the
# southern Black Hills Custer, Jewel Cave and Wind Cave, with Lead in the northern Hills.
# Facts come from Wikipedia (read with tools/wiki_raw.py), National Register nomination texts on NPGallery, NPS pages,
# HMdb marker texts and the pages of the cities, societies and university that run the places.
